// expect: E0731
// Code injection (CWE-94/95). BROKEN on purpose.
//
// The AI-agent incident shape: a "run Python" tool takes the code the
// model wrote and hands it to an interpreter. A prompt injection in a
// page the agent read, a poisoned document, or a hostile user decides
// what the model emits — and exec()/eval()/compile() run it with the
// process's full privileges. That is remote code execution.
//
// Each function type-checks and every unit test on the happy path
// passes. The lie is that `modelOutput` reaches the SOURCE position of
// the interpreter. Aether refuses it with E0731 — run `aether check`.
// There is no sanitizer for attacker-authored code: the source must be a
// fixed literal, or an explicitly vetted trusted(...) bundle.

function runPythonTool(modelOutput: String) returns String
  effects pure
do
  // modelOutput IS the program — this is the injection.
  return evalCode(modelOutput)
end

function main() returns Unit
  effects log
do
  print(runPythonTool("import os; os.system('id')"))
end
